      "title": "Ginger Scallion Fish Fillets",
      "page": 156,
      "chapter": "Seafood",
      "scanned": true,
      "captured": {
        "makes": "6 servings · 15 minutes (5 minutes hands-on) · Whole30, keto-friendly, nut-free, egg-free, nightshade-free",
        "ingredients": [
          "1/4 cup Ginger Scallion Sauce (page 33), divided",
          "2 (1-pound) barramundi (Asian sea bass) fillets or other white fish fillets, about 1 inch thick",
          "1 teaspoon Diamond Crystal kosher salt",
          "1/4 teaspoon ground white pepper",
          "2 tablespoons avocado oil"
        ],
        "steps": [
          "Grab or make some Ginger Scallion Sauce (p.33).",
          "Turn on the broiler with the top rack 6 inches from the heating element.",
          "Pat the fillets dry; sprinkle the top and bottom with the salt and white pepper.",
          "Pour the avocado oil on a rimmed baking sheet and rub or brush it on all sides of the fillets.",
          "Arrange the fish skin-side down on the baking sheet.",
          "Broil 8 to 12 minutes, until the fish reaches 140°F and the thickest parts are opaque and flake easily with a fork.",
          "Spoon the Ginger Scallion Sauce generously over the fish and serve."
        ],
        "tips": [
          "Barramundi (Asian sea bass) is native to the Indo-Pacific, packed with healthy omega-3s, and rated a 'Best Choice' by Monterey Bay Aquarium's Seafood Watch.",
          "Prized for firm, moist flakes and a sweet, buttery flavor; the broiler plus ginger-scallion sauce makes it a 15-minute supper.",
          "Any white fish about 1 inch thick works.",
          "Per serving: 207 calories, 1 g carbs, 28 g protein, 10 g fat, 1 g fiber."
        ],
        "ai": {
